</section>

<!-- TECHNICAL COMPARISON OF COMMON AEROSOL PROPELLANTS -->
<section class="section" id="technical-comparison-of-common-aerosol-propellants">
  <h2>Technical Comparison of Common Aerosol Propellants</h2>
  <p>When evaluated objectively, each propellant system offers trade-offs that must be aligned with
                application, climate, and regulatory constraints. No single propellant is superior across every
                metric — LPG and HFC hold pressure most consistently, DME contributes solvency that the others lack,
                and CO₂ and N₂ trade spray consistency for non-flammability. The table below summarizes the four
                factors formulators weigh most heavily when selecting a propellant system; see our detailed comparison
                of <a href="/compressed-vs-liquefied-gas-aerosols-pressure-profiles/">compressed gas vs liquefied gas
                aerosols</a> for the underlying pressure-profile mechanics behind these differences.</p>
